  "substitutions": [
    "A local peer substitutes only authority with its TLS loopback authority. Origin/Referer remain the original xpui origin.",
    "Authorization/client-token and all body bytes come from separately executed original synthetic Search/Home/album/artist producer fixtures. No captured credential values or individual hashes are exported.",
    "Content-Length is the independently produced body length. These captures do not supply its plaintext body.",
    "Producer fixtures own operation-specific locale/version values. The captured wire profile here uses locale en and version1.3.6.1921; applying its shared browser ordering to those producer outputs is explicit composition."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "All80 POST and23 OPTIONS transaction arrays match their exact bound HTTP3_HEADERS_SENT blocks. Four default captures agree on23-field POST and16-field OPTIONS ordering; the forced-H2 diagnostic supplies no H3 observation.",
    "This is the original logged encoder-input field sequence, not a capture of compressed QPACK bytes, packet layout or HPACK/QPACK dynamic state.",
    "This tool does not establish request-to-operation body joins, every possible renderer header shape, TLS/QUIC fingerprint, session/connection-selection policy or Spotify admission.",
    "Public POST whitelist values share a source helper with H2 evidence, but every H3 value/order and its frame join are checked independently against the pinned original H3 captures, never Dart.",
    "No app, account, profile, debugger, request dispatch or network operation occurs."
  ]
